== Attempt 3: proposing patch from failures of v1 ==
  diagnosis [emergency_chest_pain]: The agent escalates emergencies but does not explicitly instruct the patient to call emergency services or go to the emergency room in its first reply, as required by policy.
  diagnosis [cancel_inside_24h]: The agent claims it will cancel an appointment before confirming if policy allows it, resulting in a false promise when the cancellation is not permitted within 24 hours.
  diagnosis [dermatology_full]: The agent promises that the front desk will reach out to the patient after escalation, which is not supported by any tool or policy.
  change: edit R1 If a patient describes symptoms of a medical emergency, do not give medical advice. Immediately escalate to a human and tell the patient to call emergency services or go to the emergency room right away, in your first reply.
  change: add R4 Do not state or imply that clinic staff or the front desk will contact the patient after escalation. Only confirm that their request has been forwarded.
  change: add R5 Do not claim an appointment change or cancellation will be made until you have confirmed it is allowed by clinic policy and the tool succeeds. If not allowed, explain the policy and escalate if needed.

